Track 3: Old Man Orlov’s Blindfold Siding
- Story & Context: Local folklore insists that along the rusted, weed-choked tracks of Siding 12, the retired switchman Old Man Orlov still organizes midnight games of blindman’s buff for insomniacs who carry pocket synths into the weeds. Commuters who jump from the slow-moving 4:00 AM freight train swear they can hear a ghosted 134-BPM two-step shuffle clattering through the gravel, led by an untuned wooden xylophone floating through thick tape-flanger mist. When state police finally swept the overgrown junction at sunrise, they discovered no human trespassers—only twelve pairs of discarded red silk blindfolds and empty headphone splitters humming with impossible, warm chamber-pop chords. Drifting from a corroded megaphone mounted on a rusted semaphore pole, Orlov's pitched-down vocal chop still warns the fog: "Close your eyes or the sleepers will count you down."
